Fail early when nc is given no port to connect to.
nc accepts a single HOST operand so that a port can be given as
HOST:PORT, but when the host carried no port either, nc connected to
port 0, which always fails, so "nc example.com" gave a confusing
connection error such as "can't connect to remote host: Connection
refused". Resolve the address first, and if it has no port, exit with
"no port to connect to", as nc 1.10 does.

---
 networking/nc.c |    8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/networking/nc.c
+++ b/networking/nc.c
@@ -221,8 +221,14 @@
 			if (!execparam)
 				close(sfd);
 		} else {
-			cfd = create_and_connect_stream_or_die(argv[0],
+			len_and_sockaddr *lsa;
+
+			lsa = xhost2sockaddr(argv[0],
 				bb_lookup_port(argv[1], "tcp", 0));
+			/* neither a PORT operand nor HOST:PORT */
+			if (get_nport(&lsa->u.sa) == 0)
+				bb_simple_error_msg_and_die("no port to connect to");
+			cfd = xconnect_stream(lsa);
 		}
 	}
 
